From e50b6125048a1e63530f24954636547d80c7c281 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:17:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a5xx: Program the A508/A509/A512 the way Qualcomm's
 driver does

The a5xx code writes the register values captured from the A530 on every
A5xx. Qualcomm's driver for the HiBy RS6's A512 (libGLESv2_adreno.so,
read with Ghidra) and the kernel differ from them in four places, and
the RS6 shows two of them as bugs: tiled corruption on the lock screen
when blits take the 3D path (FD_MESA_DEBUG=noblit), and UI elements
that vanish for a frame when they take the 2D engine.

Highest bank bit. Tiled addresses are swizzled by the highest DDR bank
bit, which the RB, TPL1 and UCHE each carry in a mode register as
(bit - 13). The kernel programs all three at boot from the SoC's memory
configuration: 15 on msm8996, where the A530 values came from, 14 on
SDM660. fd5_emit_restore writes RB_MODE_CNTL 0x44 and TPL1_MODE_CNTL
0x544, and the blitter setup 0x4 and 0x344, all encoding bit 15, while
the UCHE keeps the kernel's 14 (UCHE_DBG_ECO_CNTL_2 on A509/A512/A540),
so the units disagree about where a tile lives. Qualcomm's driver
computes both registers from the bank bit it gets from kgsl
(A5xContext::InitStaticState: 0x40 | ((hbb+3)&3) << 1 and
0x444 | ((hbb+3)&3) << 7, so 0x42 and 0x4c4 on the RS6). Ask the kernel
for MSM_PARAM_HIGHEST_BANK_BIT, fall back to the GPU table's value, and
derive the two registers from it.

ECO bits. Qualcomm's driver (A5xWorkarounds, errata 97) and the kernel
(ADRENO_QUIRK_DISABLE_RB_DP2CLOCKGATING) both set RB_DBG_ECO_CNTL bit 9
on the A505/A506/A508/A509/A512, which the restore sequence then
cleared with the A530's 0x00100000. SP_DBG_ECO_CNTL bit 30 (errata 54)
is applied to the A510 and A530 only; every other A5xx, the A540 that
this code already special-cased included, gets 0x800.

2D copies. A5xBltDevice::A5xSelectA2DCopyMode returns the SCALE mode
for the A508, A509 and A512 unconditionally: Qualcomm's driver never
issues a plain BLIT_OP_COPY in render mode BLIT2D on them, which is the
operation freedreno used for every 2D blit, and what wrote nothing on
A508 between linear surfaces. A SCALE blit (render mode BLIT2DSCALE,
CP_BLIT op 3) reads its source through the TP, from a texture
descriptor at 0x2000 that is the ancestor of a6xx's SP_PS_2D_SRC, and
converts through an intermediate format named in the BLIT_CNTLs and
SP_2D_DST_FORMAT (0x2040). Emit copies in that form on these three
GPUs, for same-format blits of texture formats (Qualcomm's driver
refuses format conversions on them too) and for buffers, and leave the
rest to u_blitter. The A508 linear-to-linear check this replaces is no
longer reached.

Post-blit sync. After every 2D-engine blit Qualcomm's driver issues
PC_CCU_FLUSH_COLOR_TS twice, PC_CCU_INVALIDATE_COLOR,
PC_CCU_INVALIDATE_DEPTH and a wait for idle
(A5xBltDevice::HwExecPostBltSync); do the same.

